<title>USA: Haven Bancorp Inc Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>Haven Bancorp Inc Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>WOODHAVEN, N.Y. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Statements of Operations</p>
<p>		    (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				    Three Months Ended    Years Ended</p>
<p>					December 31,	 December 31,</p>
<p>					 1996    1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Total Interest Income	 28,372  26,005  109,253   96,434</p>
<p> Total Interest Expense	15,829  15,119   61,368   55,115</p>
<p> Total Non-Interest Income    2,366   3,181    9,554    9,022</p>
<p> Net income			 3,464   2,645    9,425    8,544</p>
<p>Net income per common share:</p>
<p> Primary			     0.78    0.58     2.12     1.89</p>
<p> Fully Diluted		     0.78    0.58     2.11     1.87</p>
<p>NOTE: The 1996 results included a one-time assessment of $6.8 million to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund (SAIF). Excluding the SAIF assessment charge, earnings for 1996 would have been $13.5 million, or $3.03 per share, $3.01 per share fully-diluted.</p>
<p>In the fourth quarter of 1996, Haven recorded the benefit of a change in the method it used for determining the federal tax return treatment of its bad debt reserve, which resulted in a reduction in its effective tax rate for the quarter and the year.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
